{"animath":"0.1","title":"Plate tectonics: giant slabs on the move","level":"primary","subject":"geography","topic":"plate-tectonics","kind":"concept","canvas":{"width":960,"height":540},"scenes":[{"id":"s1","caption":"Two giant plates of rock sit apart","narration":"The Earth's crust is made of giant slabs of rock called plates. Year after year, they drift.","duration_ms":6000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateA","kind":"polygon","points":[[120,400],[120,300],[420,300],[420,400]],"fill":"#c9a06a","stroke":"#7a5a30","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"Plate A: a giant slab of the Earth's crust."}},{"at_ms":300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateB","kind":"polygon","points":[[540,400],[540,300],[840,300],[840,400]],"fill":"#a8b98a","stroke":"#5a6b3a","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"Plate B: another slab, sitting apart from Plate A."}},{"at_ms":600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"aLabel","kind":"text","x":230,"y":240,"text":"Plate A","size":32,"color":"#6b4d22","explain":"Label: Plate A."}},{"at_ms":800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"bLabel","kind":"text","x":650,"y":240,"text":"Plate B","size":32,"color":"#445522","explain":"Label: Plate B."}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"move","target":"plateA","to":{"points":[[140,400],[140,300],[440,300],[440,400]]},"dur_ms":2000},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"move","target":"plateB","to":{"points":[[520,400],[520,300],[820,300],[820,400]]},"dur_ms":2000},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"caption","text":"Year after year, the plates drift towards each other"}]},{"id":"s2","caption":"The plates push together","narration":"The drift becomes a push. The two plates collide head-on.","duration_ms":7000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateA2","kind":"polygon","points":[[160,400],[160,300],[430,300],[430,400]],"fill":"#c9a06a","stroke":"#7a5a30","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"Plate A: still moving towards Plate B."}},{"at_ms":300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateB2","kind":"polygon","points":[[530,400],[530,300],[800,300],[800,400]],"fill":"#a8b98a","stroke":"#5a6b3a","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"Plate B: still moving towards Plate A."}},{"at_ms":700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pushL","kind":"arrow","x1":100,"y1":350,"x2":150,"y2":350,"stroke":"#d35400","width":5,"explain":"Push: Plate A is driven towards Plate B."}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pushR","kind":"arrow","x1":860,"y1":350,"x2":810,"y2":350,"stroke":"#d35400","width":5,"explain":"Push: Plate B is driven towards Plate A."}},{"at_ms":1300,"do":"move","target":"plateA2","to":{"points":[[330,400],[330,300],[600,300],[600,400]]},"dur_ms":2500},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"move","target":"plateB2","to":{"points":[[600,400],[600,300],[870,300],[870,400]]},"dur_ms":2500},{"at_ms":4500,"do":"caption","text":"The two plates collide"}]},{"id":"s3","caption":"One plate slides under the other","narration":"Where they meet, the denser plate is forced down and slides underneath. That sinking is called subduction.","duration_ms":7000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateC","kind":"polygon","points":[[200,380],[200,300],[560,300],[560,380]],"fill":"#c9a06a","stroke":"#7a5a30","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"The lighter plate: it rides on top."}},{"at_ms":300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateD","kind":"polygon","points":[[560,380],[560,300],[880,300],[880,380]],"fill":"#a8b98a","stroke":"#5a6b3a","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"The denser plate: it is about to slide underneath."}},{"at_ms":800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dive","kind":"arrow","x1":700,"y1":290,"x2":640,"y2":430,"stroke":"#d35400","width":5,"explain":"Down: the denser plate dives below the other."}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"move","target":"plateD","to":{"points":[[520,470],[520,390],[840,390],[840,470]]},"dur_ms":2200},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"caption","text":"This sinking is called subduction"}]},{"id":"s4","caption":"Plates creep, they never lurch","narration":"Do not imagine a sudden jolt. Real plates move only about two centimetres a year - slower than your fingernails grow.","duration_ms":6000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"plateE","kind":"polygon","points":[[200,400],[200,310],[500,310],[500,400]],"fill":"#c9a06a","stroke":"#7a5a30","strokeWidth":3,"explain":"A plate: it moves only centimetres a year."}},{"at_ms":300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"marker","kind":"circle","cx":350,"cy":355,"r":10,"fill":"#d35400","stroke":"#7a2a00","strokeWidth":2,"explain":"A marker: watch how far it travels in a year."}},{"at_ms":500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"rate","kind":"text","x":560,"y":370,"text":"2 cm per year","size":30,"color":"#7a3a00","explain":"Label: real plates move about 2 cm per year."}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"move","target":"marker","to":{"cx":358,"cy":355},"dur_ms":3000},{"at_ms":4700,"do":"caption","text":"Plates creep centimetres a year - never a sudden lurch"}]}]}
